# Sound regression checks

Run from the workspace root in WSL:

```bash
bash system/tests/check-media.sh sdl-sound
bash system/tests/check-media.sh mace
bash system/tests/check-media.sh pcm
```

The SDL test exercises playback, stop while a callback is waiting, idle silence,
restart and worker shutdown. The MACE test checks reference PCM hashes, stereo
downmix, output bounds and invalid packets. Its xorshift input starts at
0x12345678 and contains 2048 bytes. Golden hashes were generated by FFmpeg 6.1.1
using AIFF-C MAC3/MAC6 fixtures and unsigned 8-bit PCM output, without resampling.
Math Rabbit's intro was also compared byte-for-byte against FFmpeg's output.
No app resources or external decoder programs are needed to run these tests.

The PCM checks cover unsigned 8-bit and signed big-endian 16-bit mono/stereo
conversion, downmixing, guards, truncated input and invalid formats under Linux
ASan/UBSan. Extended sound headers use numFrames and sampleSize rather than
treating numChannels as a byte count. The staged PPC Sound Probe queues thirty-two
1024-frame stereo buffers, verifies callback completion and checks that playback
takes time; discarding every buffer immediately fails that check. Output still
uses the existing unsigned 8-bit mono mixer and resampler.

MACE decoding is adapted from FFmpeg libavcodec/mace.c at commit
aafb5c655edc76a753275c383ebb139feb032718:
https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/aafb5c655edc76a753275c383ebb139feb032718/libavcodec/mace.c
The decoder retains its LGPL 2.1-or-later notice. The license is distributed in
COPYING.LGPLv2.1 and beside the staged ROMAW.exe. The runtime does not
depend on FFmpeg libraries. Note-synth commands currently use square-wave
tones; arbitrary instrument and wave-table synthesis is not implemented.

Classic .Sound driver writes (reference -4) support free-form sample buffers and
four-tone tables through the same mixer as Sound Manager channels. The
legacy_sound_test.c fixture, included in check-runtime.sh robustness, checks sample
stepping, live waveforms, duration, tagged 24-bit pointers, sync/async completion,
KillIO, launch cleanup and invalid spans. It captures PCM without opening host
audio. StuntCopter was also tested interactively and confirmed audible. Legacy
square-wave synthesizer records are not implemented; they return paramErr.
